* MS-20-style VCF — OTA revision (later MS20s, KLM-307 daughterboard)
* ==========================================================================
* The voltage-controlled lowpass filter from the later Korg MS-20. The early
* MS-20 (and the MS-10) used a Korg-proprietary resin-sealed module, the
* "Korg-35", built around transistors run in *reverse* saturation as
* current-controlled resistors. Korg redesigned the filter for later MS-20s
* around the LM13600 OTA — that OTA revision is what this netlist models.
*
* SOURCE SCHEMATIC
*   Timothy E. Stinchcombe, "A Study of the Korg MS10 & MS20 Filters",
*   <https://www.timstinchcombe.co.uk/synth/MS20_study.pdf>, Figure 2
*   ("OTA-based version of later MS20s") and the §2.1 transfer-function
*   derivation. Every R / C value and the device count below is read off
*   that figure. Stinchcombe in turn transcribed it from the readable
*   KLM-307 daughterboard schematic. The OTA-revision MS-20 filter is also
*   documented by Rene Schmitz (<https://www.schmitzbits.de/ms20.html>) and
*   Eddy Bergman's MS-20 filter build — both corroborate the topology.
*
* WHAT THE OTA MS-20 ACTUALLY IS — and the modelling choices here
* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Stinchcombe's key finding (§1, §2.1): the OTA MS-20 filter is NOT a true
* Sallen-Key — it is "two cascaded, buffered first-order sections". Each
* section is an OTA whose transconductance replaces the section resistor:
*   - OTA `X1` (LM13600 half) + cap C4 = first 1-pole lowpass section.
*   - A unity-gain buffer follows X1's output (this buffer is the structural
*     difference from a real Sallen-Key — it removes the inter-stage loading).
*   - OTA `X2` (LM13600 half) + cap C5 = second 1-pole lowpass section.
*   - Global resonance feedback (`k2`) is taken from the output back to the
*     first section's "+" reference, via a non-inverting op-amp gain stage.
*
* Stinchcombe §2.1, eq. (3)-(5): each OTA section behaves as a simple RC
* section with the resistor set by the OTA. With `Vin'` the OTA non-inverting
* input, `R1`/`R2` the input attenuator (R20/R21 = 220R here) and `R3` the
* OTA feedback (R22 = 10k):
*       i_o = 19.2*Iabc*(V+ - V-)            (LM13600 transconductance)
*       omega_c = K*k / C,  K = 19.2*Iabc,  k ~= R2/R1   (input attenuation)
* and the complete closed-loop transfer function is the standard biquad
*       Vo/Vin = -k1 / ( s^2/wc^2 + (2 - k1*k2)*s/wc + 1 )
* with k1 = 1 (the inter-stage buffer gain) and k2 the resonance-feedback
* gain. Self-oscillation at k2 -> 2/k1 = 2.
*
* circuit-runtime mapping. circuit-runtime has a first-class OTA device
* (the `O` card — `Iout = Iabc*tanh(Vin/2Vt)` + output rail-current
* starvation), the exact LM13600/CA3080 behavioural model already used by
* `svf-ota.cir`, `wasp-filter.cir` and `efm-3521-vcf.cir`. The two LM13600
* halves -> two `O` cards. The inter-stage unity buffer and the resonance
* op-amp -> `A`-card op-amps (the real X1 buffer is a discrete JFET+op-amp
* follower; X5 is a uA741). The MS-20's resonance-feedback diode clamp
* (D8-D13, six 1N4148 in three anti-parallel pairs across the feedback
* resistor) -> `D` cards: this is the MS-20's signature — the diodes bound
* self-oscillation and add the amplitude-dependent screaming-resonance
* distortion the filter is famous for, exactly the role the 1N4148 clamp
* plays in `sem-filter.cir`.
*
* NOTE ON THE OTA TRANSCONDUCTANCE SCALING
*   The real LM13600 has gm = 19.2*Iabc. circuit-runtime's OTA model uses the
*   physical gm = Iabc/(2*Vt) ~= 19.34*Iabc at Vt=25.85mV. Each OTA reads
*   its input and its own (buffered) output through matched 10k/220R
*   attenuators (k = 220/10220 = 0.0215), so the differential stays in the
*   OTA's linear +-20 mV range and each section is a unity-gain 1-pole
*   lowpass with omega_c = 19.34*Iabc*k/C:
*       fc = 3.01e7 * Iabc   (Hz per A)  ->  1 kHz at 33 uA, 15 kHz at 0.5 mA
*   So the cutoff knob moves the corner and the passband stays at 0 dB.
*   (2026-10-08 fix: the previous netlist had no local feedback on either
*   OTA, so both sections were bare integrators whose corner was set by the
*   resonance pot's load; IABC only changed the gain.)
*
* TOPOLOGY (node by node — Stinchcombe Fig. 2 / eq. 3-5)
* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*   Section 1: OTA `O1`, + input = attenuated `in` (R_in/R_ia), - input =
*       attenuated buffered output `v2b` (R_f1/R_f1a). Charges C1 on `v2`.
*       C1's far end returns to the resonance feedback node `resamp`
*       (k2*Vo), the MS-20's bootstrapped-capacitor resonance:
*         v2 = H*x + (s/wc)*H*k2*Vo,  H = 1/(1 + s/wc)
*   Inter-stage buffer `Abuf` (the JFET follower): `v2` -> `v2b`.
*   Section 2: OTA `O2`, + = attenuated `v2b`, - = attenuated `vob`,
*       charges C2 on `vo`; `Aout` buffers `vo` -> `vob` (the filter output).
*   Closed loop: Vo/Vin = 1 / (s^2/wc^2 + (2 - k2)*s/wc + 1), Stinchcombe's
*       biquad with k1 = 1: Q = 1/(2 - k2), self-oscillation at k2 = 2.
*   Resonance: `vob` -> R_res -> VR1 pot -> non-inverting gain stage `Ares`
*       (1 + 10k/3.3k ~= 4) with the D8-D13 diode string across its 10k
*       feedback resistor -> `resamp`. k2 = 4.03 * 47k/(39k+47k) * RES_K
*       ~= 2.2 * RES_K, so the filter self-oscillates near RES_K = 0.9; the
*       diodes bound the oscillation and add the MS-20 scream.
*
* HARDWARE MAPPING
*   OTAs   <- one LM13600 dual (X1, X2 — two halves, shared cutoff bias).
*   Buffers<- the discrete JFET-input follower at X1's output, and the
*             output buffer.
*   Op-amp <- uA741 (X5) resonance gain stage.
*   Diodes <- D8-D13, six 1N4148 (three anti-parallel pairs) across the
*             resonance stage's feedback resistor.
*   Caps   <- C4 = C5 = 2.2 nF (the two 1-pole section caps, schematic).
* ==========================================================================

* --- Cutoff / resonance controls ------------------------------------------
* IABC : LM13600 bias current (A), shared by both OTA sections so the two
*        1-pole corners track: fc = 3.01e7 * IABC. In hardware this is the
*        cutoff CV through the expo converter.
* RES_K: resonance pot 0..1; self-oscillation from ~0.9.
.param IABC  = 33u      ; OTA bias current — corner ~1 kHz
.param RES_K = 0.5      ; resonance pot (k2 ~= 2.2*RES_K, Q ~= 1.1 here)

* --- Supplies — the MS-20 filter board's +/-12 V rails --------------------
Vpos  vpos  0   DC  12
Vneg  vneg  0   DC -12

* --- Cutoff-CV bias-current nodes -----------------------------------------
* Each OTA reads its `cv` node voltage directly as a bias current in amperes.
Vcv1  cv1   0   DC {IABC}
Vcv2  cv2   0   DC {IABC}

* --- Input ----------------------------------------------------------------
.param F = 220
Vref vr 0 DC 2.5
G1 0 ramp vr 0 {F/12500}
C1  ramp 0 50n IC=0
S1  ramp 0 ramp 0 SW_SCH
A1  ramp vco vco opamp_buf
Rload vco 0 100k
Rd1 vco d1 10k
Rd2 d1 0 1k
Cc  d1 ac 100n
Rac ac 0 100k
Vin   in    0   AC 1 0   SIN(0 0.2 220)

* --- Section 1: OTA 1-pole lowpass — output `v2`, buffered `v2b` ----------
R_in  in    s1in  10k               ; input attenuator (R19 / R20)
R_ia  s1in  0     220
R_f1  v2b   n1    10k               ; local feedback attenuator (R22)
R_f1a n1    0     220
O1    s1in  n1    cv1   v2    LM13600
C1    v2    resamp  2.2n            ; C4, far end on the resonance feedback
Abuf  v2    v2b   v2b   opamp_buf   ; the JFET follower: "not a Sallen-Key"

* --- Section 2: OTA 1-pole lowpass — output `vo`, buffered `vob` ----------
R_i2  v2b   s2in  10k
R_i2a s2in  0     220
R_f2  vob   n2    10k
R_f2a n2    0     220
O2    s2in  n2    cv2   vo    LM13600
C2    vo    0     2.2n              ; C5
Aout  vo    vob   vob   opamp_buf   ; output buffer — the lowpass output

* --- Resonance loop: output -> pot -> gain + diode clamp -> C1 -------------
R_res vob   rwiper  39k
Rp_a  rwiper  rfb_in  {47k*(1-RES_K)+1}   ; VR1 pot: output end -> wiper
Rp_b  rfb_in  0       {47k*RES_K+1}       ; VR1 pot: wiper -> ground
* Non-inverting gain stage (X5 uA741): gain = 1 + R_rg/R_rf ~= 4.
Ares  rfb_in  rgain   resamp  opamp_res
R_rg  resamp  rgain   10k
R_rf  rgain   0       3.3k
* D8-D13 across R_rg: past ~3 diode drops the stage's gain collapses, which
* bounds self-oscillation and gives the amplitude-dependent MS-20 scream.
D_p1  resamp  dn1     D1N4148
D_n1  dn1     resamp  D1N4148
D_p2  dn1     dn2     D1N4148
D_n2  dn2     dn1     D1N4148
D_p3  dn2     rgain   D1N4148
D_n3  rgain   dn2     D1N4148

* --- LM13600 OTA model -----------------------------------------------------
* circuit-runtime's OTA device: Iout = Iabc*tanh(Vin/2Vt) input
* transconductance + exponential output rail-current starvation. The MS-20's
* LM13600 is the same behavioural part as the CA3080 used elsewhere in the
* corpus; run here on the +/-12 V MS-20 rails.
.model LM13600 OTA (IS=1e-14 VT=0.02585 VPOS=12 VNEG=-12 VDROPPOS=1.5 VDROPNEG=1.5)

* --- Op-amp models ---------------------------------------------------------
* The inter-stage unity buffer and the uA741 resonance gain stage. 1-pole
* macromodels with output rail-clip; `vsat=11` keeps them inside +/-12 V.
.model opamp_buf OPAMP (aol=1e5 gbp=1e6 rin=1e12 rout=100 vsat=11)
.model opamp_res OPAMP (aol=2e5 gbp=1e6 rin=1e12 rout=75  vsat=11)

* --- 1N4148 small-signal silicon diode (resonance clamp) -------------------
.model SW_SCH SW (Vt=2.5 Vh=2.0 Ron=10 Roff=10Meg)
.model D1N4148 D (IS=2.52n N=1.752 RS=0.568)

* --- circuit-runtime playback annotations ---------------------------------
* `;@` lines are read by circuit-runtime's `--play` mode and ignored by
* ngspice. `;@input` retunes the Vin SIN frequency from a MIDI note;
* `;@output` is the lowpass node `vo`. The default params (corner ~1 kHz,
* moderate resonance) play a 220 Hz note through the MS-20 lowpass.
;@input  midi.note → freq(Vin)
;@output vob

* --- Analysis (ngspice) ----------------------------------------------------
;@output vob

.control
tran 20u 50m UIC
.endc


